cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use TabFlux, please cite it as below. A Zenodo DOI is minted with the first public release and replaces the repository URL."
title: "TabFlux: machine-learning classification of microbial community profiles"
type: software
version: 1.6.0
date-released: 2026-09-28
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/iLivius/TabFlux"
authors:
  - family-names: Antonielli
    given-names: Livio
    affiliation: "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"
    email: livio.antonielli@ait.ac.at
  - family-names: Pucher
    given-names: Lukas
    affiliation: "AIT Austrian Institute of Technology"
keywords:
  - microbiome
  - machine learning
  - mlr3
  - TabPFN
  - nested resampling
  - leave-one-dataset-out
abstract: >-
  TabFlux turns a microbiome table into an honestly evaluated classifier. It
  aggregates taxa to any rank, normalises sequencing depth, selects features
  and tunes hyperparameters inside every fold of a grouped, nested evaluation
  (whole studies, sites or batches held out together; leave-one-dataset-out is
  one option), then reports per-group performance, probability calibration and
  SHAP explanations. It runs on the public curated Food Metagenomic Data
  repository out of the box.
